
                                                   WRITEADDRESS COMMAND


WRITEADDRESS command can be used to write data to a hex file at a particular address. 

Below is the syntax :
                                  writeaddress -addr address  [-val {data}] 

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -addr       |    Takes address value such as 0x80000000. Mandatory switch.
   -val        |    Specifies the value to be written. Mandatory switch.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
    read -in input.hex        
    writeaddress -addr 0x80802000 -val 0xAE123411
    write -out outputFile.hex -lyt 0x10
    